---
import CompetitorComparison from '../../components/compare/CompetitorComparison.astro';

// Competitor cells reflect GoRoadie's own public pages and app-store listings, checked 16 Oct 2026:
//   goroadie.com/pro (mobile diary for ADIs/PDIs, companion learner app, three reminders per lesson
//     by text/email/in-app, Stripe payments, expenses + receipt scanning, "Making Tax Digital ready",
//     Theory Test Pro / 4-in-1 theory progress, lesson-request link and enquiry manager)
//   goroadie.com/schools (separate multi-instructor product, demo on request)
//   goroadie.com and /instructors (learner referral marketplace, pay per pupil)
//   App Store id1548955079, Google Play com.goroadie.pro (iOS and Android; no web version listed)
// GoRoadie's page gives two different trial lengths, so we state neither.
// 2 Nov 2026: re-checked goroadie.com/pro. Same features; it also says "zero text costs"
//   for reminders. Name is written "GoRoadie" (one word), the instructor app "GoRoadie Pro".
// 9 Nov 2026: re-checked goroadie.com/pro, the /pro/help guides and the Sept 2026 press release:
//   /pro/help/how-to-add-a-lesson ("Lesson Preview highlights conflicts, even from connected, external
//     calendars"); /pro (External Calendar Sync; "Fill Nearby Open Slots", first come first served;
//     FAQ "Can pupils see or book into my diary? No.")
//   /pro/help (add teaching vehicles to lessons; schedule a driving test or mock test)
//   /press/2026-09-goroadie-preps-autumn-update ("Web Dashboard > Finances > Integrations" for QuickBooks;
//     mileage "on the web for easy access on desktop"; group messaging "from the web")
// "Not listed" = not found on those pages; never "No" unless the vendor says so.
const rows = [
  { label: 'AI lesson briefings', values: [true, 'Not listed'] },
  { label: 'DVSA 27-skill, 8-category progress tracking', values: [true, 'Progress tracking and reflective logs; DVSA skills not named'] },
  { label: 'Theory test progress shown alongside lessons', values: [false, 'Yes (Theory Test Pro, 4-in-1)'] },
  { label: 'Automatic lesson reminders', values: ['Email', 'Yes (text, email and in-app; no text costs)'] },
  { label: 'WhatsApp reminders', values: ['Coming soon', 'Not listed'] },
  { label: 'Pupils book online from your website', values: [true, "Lesson-request link and enquiry manager; GoRoadie says pupils can't book into your diary"] },
  { label: 'Works in a web browser on a computer', values: [true, 'Web Dashboard listed (finances, mileage, messaging); diary in a browser not stated'] },
  { label: 'Pupil app or portal', values: ['Yes (iOS, Android or web)', 'Yes (free learner app)'] },
  { label: 'Clash checks across pupil, instructor and vehicle', values: [true, 'Conflict alerts, including connected calendars; vehicles not stated'] },
  { label: 'Google / Apple Calendar', values: [false, 'Yes (syncs with your phone calendar)'] },
  { label: 'Cancellation-gap broadcast to pupils', values: [false, 'Yes (offer an open slot to nearby pupils)'] },
  { label: 'Test bookings and results recording (coming soon)', values: ['Coming soon', 'Driving and mock tests added to the diary; results not stated'] },
  { label: 'Vehicle MOT, tax and insurance tracking', values: [true, 'Not listed (vehicles can be assigned to lessons)'] },
  { label: 'Card payments through Stripe', values: [true, true] },
  { label: 'Expenses and receipt scanning', values: [false, 'Yes (plus mileage and QuickBooks; "Making Tax Digital ready")'] },
  { label: 'Multi-instructor schools in the same product', values: [true, 'Separate GoRoadie Schools product (demo on request)'] },
  { label: 'Learner marketplace and leads', values: [false, 'Yes (GoRoadie marketplace, pay per pupil)'] },
  { label: 'Permanent free plan', values: ['Yes, from 1 April 2027 (free until then)', 'Free for trainee instructors (PDIs); free trial for ADIs'] },
];

const faqs = [
  {
    question: 'What is a good alternative to GoRoadie Pro?',
    answer: "For UK driving instructors the main alternatives are Total Drive (offline diary, branded pupil app, Smart Gaps, theory suite), MyDriveTime (diary and admin app with a student app, SMS reminders on its individual plan and expense receipts), Lesson Diary (browser and iPhone app built around filling cancellations) and DriveSchoolPro (DVSA 27-skill tracking, AI lesson briefings, Stripe card payments and a web version, free until 31 March 2027). None of these runs a learner marketplace like GoRoadie's, so if new pupils are why you use it, weigh that first.",
    links: [{ text: 'Total Drive vs DriveSchoolPro', url: '/compare/total-drive/' }, { text: 'MyDriveTime vs DriveSchoolPro', url: '/compare/my-drive-time/' }],
  },
  {
    question: 'What is GoRoadie?',
    answer: "GoRoadie is a UK driving company with two sides. Its website, goroadie.com, is a marketplace where learner drivers find an instructor, and instructors pay per pupil they take on. GoRoadie Pro is its separate iPhone and Android app for instructors (ADIs and PDIs), with a diary, a free learner app, reminders, card payments and expense tracking, plus a Web Dashboard mentioned for finances, mileage and messaging. This page compares GoRoadie Pro with DriveSchoolPro.",
    links: [{ text: 'GoRoadie Pro', url: 'https://goroadie.com/pro' }],
  },
  {
    question: 'Can I use GoRoadie Pro on a computer?',
    answer: "Partly, going by its own site. GoRoadie Pro is an iPhone, iPad and Android app, and its September 2026 update notes mention a Web Dashboard for finances (including a QuickBooks connection), mileage and group messaging. We couldn't find whether the diary itself runs in a browser. DriveSchoolPro works in any web browser as well as on iPhone and Android, so you can plan the week on a laptop and run the day from your phone.",
    links: [{ text: 'DriveSchoolPro for driving instructors', url: '/driving-instructor-software/' }],
  },
  {
    question: 'Does either track the DVSA 27 skills?',
    answer: "DriveSchoolPro tracks all 27 DVSA skills in 8 categories, lesson by lesson, and pupils see their own progress. GoRoadie Pro lists pupil progress tracking and reflective logs, and shows pupils' theory test progress, which DriveSchoolPro doesn't. It doesn't name the DVSA skills.",
    links: [{ text: 'How DriveSchoolPro tracks progress', url: '/how-progress-works/' }],
  },
  {
    question: 'GoRoadie helps me find new pupils. Does DriveSchoolPro?',
    answer: "No. GoRoadie runs a marketplace where learners are matched with instructors, who pay per pupil they accept. DriveSchoolPro has no marketplace. It gives you a booking widget for your own website and a Google review request ready to send when a pupil passes, which helps people find you on Google.",
    links: [{ text: 'Review requests in DriveSchoolPro', url: '/features/reviews/' }],
  },
  {
    question: 'Which handles Making Tax Digital?',
    answer: "GoRoadie Pro says its expense capture is Making Tax Digital ready, and lists mileage tracking and a QuickBooks integration. DriveSchoolPro records lesson income, invoices and payments but doesn't track expenses or file anything with HMRC, so you'd pair it with accounting software. Our guide explains who needs MTD from April 2027.",
    links: [{ text: 'Making Tax Digital for driving instructors', url: '/blog/making-tax-digital-driving-instructors/' }],
  },
  {
    question: 'Is this a fair comparison?',
    answer: "We've tried to make it one. The GoRoadie column only records what GoRoadie's own website and app-store listings say, first checked on 16 October 2026 and re-checked, including its help guides, on 9 November 2026. Where we couldn't find a feature we say \"Not listed\", not \"No\". We don't quote GoRoadie's prices because they change, so use its own page. If you spot an error, email info@driveschoolpro.com and we'll correct it.",
    links: [{ text: 'GoRoadie Pro', url: 'https://goroadie.com/pro' }],
  },
];
---

<CompetitorComparison
  competitor={{ name: 'GoRoadie', alternateName: 'GoRoadie Pro', slug: 'goroadie', pricingUrl: 'https://goroadie.com/pro' }}
  h1="GoRoadie vs DriveSchoolPro"
  seo={{
    title: 'GoRoadie Pro vs DriveSchoolPro, and Alternatives (UK, 2026)',
    description: 'GoRoadie Pro vs DriveSchoolPro feature by feature, plus UK GoRoadie alternatives: Total Drive, MyDriveTime and Lesson Diary. Free until 31 March 2027.',
    schemaDescription: 'Feature-by-feature comparison of DriveSchoolPro and GoRoadie Pro for UK driving instructors, including what DriveSchoolPro does not do.',
    datePublished: '2026-10-16',
    dateModified: '2026-11-09',
  }}
  checkedOn="9 November 2026"
  heroIntro="A plain, feature-by-feature comparison for UK instructors weighing up GoRoadie Pro. It covers what's different, and what DriveSchoolPro doesn't do."
  featuredAnswer="DriveSchoolPro and GoRoadie Pro are both UK apps for driving instructors, with a diary, a free pupil app, reminders and Stripe card payments. DriveSchoolPro adds DVSA 27-skill tracking, AI lesson briefings, online booking from your website, vehicle MOT, tax and insurance tracking, and multi-instructor schools in the same product. GoRoadie Pro adds text-message reminders, phone calendar sync, open-slot offers to nearby pupils, expense and receipt tracking, pupils' theory test progress and access to GoRoadie's learner marketplace."
  intro="This page is for an instructor looking at GoRoadie Pro and wondering whether DriveSchoolPro is worth a look too. GoRoadie Pro is a UK app with features we don't have, so this isn't a case against it. It's a list of what's different."
  rows={rows}
  switchHeading="Where DriveSchoolPro differs"
  switchIntro="These are the differences that exist today, from the table above."
  switchItems={[
    {
      title: 'The full DVSA framework',
      body: "DriveSchoolPro tracks the official 27 skills across 8 categories, lesson by lesson, and pupils see their own progress in their app. GoRoadie Pro lists general progress tracking and reflective logs.",
    },
    {
      title: 'Lesson prep written for you',
      body: "Before each lesson, DriveSchoolPro writes a short briefing from your last notes and the pupil's skill ratings, using Claude. We couldn't find an equivalent on GoRoadie's site.",
    },
    {
      title: 'Phone, tablet and computer',
      body: "DriveSchoolPro runs on iPhone, Android and in any web browser, so the same diary is on your laptop at home and your phone in the car. GoRoadie Pro is a phone and tablet app; its site mentions a Web Dashboard for finances, mileage and messaging, but not the diary.",
    },
    {
      title: 'Grows into a school',
      body: 'Add instructors to the same account when you take someone on, with role-based access and vehicle tracking. GoRoadie offers schools a separate product.',
    },
    {
      title: 'A permanent free plan',
      body: "DriveSchoolPro is free until 31 March 2027 with no card. From 1 April 2027 there's a permanent Free plan (1 instructor, up to 60 lessons a month), Solo at £22 a month, or School at £22 a month plus £10 per extra instructor, with no VAT charged.",
    },
  ]}
  gapsHeading="What DriveSchoolPro doesn't do"
  gapsBody="DriveSchoolPro has no learner marketplace, so it won't bring you new pupils the way GoRoadie can. We don't track expenses or scan receipts, so you'll need accounting software for that side of your tax return. We don't show pupils' theory test progress. We have no phone calendar sync and can't offer a cancelled slot to other pupils; GoRoadie Pro lists both. Lesson reminders go out by email only for now (WhatsApp is coming soon), where GoRoadie Pro also sends texts. Recording test bookings and results is coming soon, where GoRoadie Pro already puts driving and mock tests in the diary. If any of these decides it for you, that's a fair reason to choose GoRoadie Pro."
  sources={[
    { label: 'GoRoadie Pro', url: 'https://goroadie.com/pro' },
    { label: 'GoRoadie Pro help and tutorials', url: 'https://www.goroadie.com/pro/help' },
    { label: 'GoRoadie Pro help: adding a lesson (conflict highlighting)', url: 'https://www.goroadie.com/pro/help/how-to-add-a-lesson' },
    { label: 'GoRoadie Pro help: adding a driving or mock test', url: 'https://www.goroadie.com/pro/help/how-to-add-a-driving-test-or-mock-test' },
    { label: 'GoRoadie 2026 Autumn update (Web Dashboard, QuickBooks, mileage)', url: 'https://www.goroadie.com/press/2026-09-goroadie-preps-autumn-update' },
    { label: 'GoRoadie Schools', url: 'https://goroadie.com/schools' },
    { label: 'GoRoadie: for instructors', url: 'https://goroadie.com/instructors' },
    { label: 'GoRoadie Pro on the App Store', url: 'https://apps.apple.com/gb/app/goroadie-pro/id1548955079' },
    { label: 'GoRoadie Pro on Google Play', url: 'https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=com.goroadie.pro' },
    { label: 'Lesson Diary home page (alternatives list, checked 3 November 2026)', url: 'https://lessondiary.co.uk/' },
  ]}
  alternativesKey="goroadie"
  faqs={faqs}
  faqTitle="DriveSchoolPro vs GoRoadie Pro: common questions"
  updates={[{ date: '9 November 2026', text: 'checked again, including GoRoadie\'s help guides and news. We corrected two cells: GoRoadie Pro flags lesson clashes, including with connected calendars, and it lists a Web Dashboard for finances and mileage. We also added its calendar sync, open-slot offers to nearby pupils and test scheduling.' }]}
/>
